.TH NERD-CHAT-GUI 1 "2026-11-09" "sine-loco 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sine-loco-gui \- serverless chat over Tor onion services (graphical version)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sine-loco-gui
[\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fB\-\-ram\fR] [\fB\-\-low\-mem\fR] [\fB\-\-tor\-control\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-\-tor\-socks\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-\-cannot\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-swap\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The graphical front end of nerd\-chat. It starts from the application menu, connects by itself and reconnects automatically. Messages exist only in memory. There is no screen\-reader support on purpose: a screen reader would receive a copy of every message. Unaudited software: read SECURITY.md in /usr/share/doc/sine-loco-gui before relying on it.
.PP
The options have the same meaning as in nerd\-chat(1). The panic button (or F12) wipes everything and exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
sine-loco(1)
